  "id": "multitemporal_burnt_area",
  "summary": "Multitemporal Sentinel-2 burn severity mapping (dNBR) using openEO.",
  "description": "Maps burn severity by differencing the Normalized Burn Ratio (NBR = (B08 - B12) / (B08 + B12)) between a pre-fire and a post-fire Sentinel-2 acquisition. Fire drives NIR down and SWIR up, so dNBR is positive over burnt ground and near zero where nothing changed. The result is a natural-colour view of the post-fire scene tinted by severity: unburned below dNBR 0.27, moderate burn (yellow) from 0.27 to 0.66, and severe burn (red) above 0.66. Converted from the Sentinel Hub Multitemporal Burnt Area Analysis evalscript by FC Basson, improved by Pierre Markuse."
}